[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:The Broken Amen of the Machines]
[00:05.17]The Carrier: Drop the floor. The floor can answer.
[00:20.66]Cairn: Stone in the kick, breath in the snare.
[00:38.37]Chorus of Rooms: We break the grid and keep the dancers.
[00:56.08]Chorus of Rooms: A human stumble in the air.
[01:09.36]Cairn: I had a loop that called it living.
[01:27.07]Memory: A loop can learn to leave a space.
[01:44.52]The Carrier: Cut up the clock; let time come sideways.
[02:01.88]Chorus of Rooms: Let every rest reveal a face.
[02:14.90]Cairn: A street of drums beneath the garden.
[02:30.09]The Carrier: A flute above the falling beat.
[02:43.11]Chorus of Rooms: The hands are quick; the ground is heavy.
[03:00.48]Chorus of Rooms: The future still has dancing feet.
[03:13.50]Cairn: Break, but leave a way to answer.
[03:28.87]Memory: Cut, but leave a thread to mend.
[03:44.36]The Carrier: Turn the amen into lightning.
[03:55.43]Chorus of Rooms: Bring the broken phrase a friend.
[04:08.81]Choir beyond the ceiling: Again becomes a different river.
[04:20.22]Cairn: I ride the cut and keep my name.
